 dway alongside Golden Globe&reg\; nominee Corey Stoll and Emmy&reg\; Award
  nominee Michael Urie in <em>Lost Lear</em>\, a deeply moving\, astonishin
 gly imaginative new play that marks the Broadway debut of writer-director 
 Dan Colley.<br /><br />As her grip on the present slips\, Joy (Chastain)\,
  a former actress\, is certain she&rsquo\;s back in rehearsal for King Lea
 r. At her care home\, her nurse (Urie) takes his cues from her\, stepping 
 into whatever role she needs him to play. When her estranged son Conor (St
 oll) comes to visit\, he&rsquo\;s ready to tell his mother what he&rsquo\;
 s spent years leaving unsaid. But if he wants her to hear him\, he&rsquo\;
 ll have to step into the scene. A limited event. A memory that will be imp
 ossible to leave behind.<br /><br />The design team for<em> Lost Lear</em>
  includes three-time Tony Award winner Scott Pask (production design)\, fi
 ve-time Tony Award nominee Heather Gilbert (lighting design)\, Tony Award 
 winner Cody Spencer (sound design)\, Tony Award winner Hana S. Kim and Yan
 a Biryukova (projection design)\, Daniel McAuley (original music)\, Junipe
 r Street Productions (production manager)\, Taylor Williams\, CSA (casting
 )\, and Rachel Bauder (production stage manager)\, with 101 Productions\, 
 Ltd./Christopher Taggart serving as general managers.</p>
LOCATION:Booth Theatre\, 222 West 45th Street\, New York NY 10036
URL:https://www.telecharge.com/Lost-Lear-Tickets
END:VEVENT
